        "name": "USN-8138-2",
        "description": "USN-8138-1 fixed a vulnerability in tar-rs. This update provides the corresponding update for Ubuntu 20.04 LTS.  Original advisory details:   It was discovered that tar-rs incorrectly handled symlinks when unpacking  a tar archive. If a user or automated system were tricked into processing  a specially crafted tar archive, a remote attacker could use this issue to  modify permissions of arbitrary directories outside the extraction root,  and possibly escalate privileges.",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2026-33056"
        ]
      },
